## 8. Design Decisions (RESOLVED — ratified by David 2026-07-29)

### [DD-LB-LAUNCH-MECHANISM] Launch by intent-publish (recommended) vs direct launcher-spawn

- decision: how a tile press reaches a running app.
- chosen: intent-publish + ONE generalized `target->scene` launcher parameterized by a data table (NOT six sibling launchers) — the narrow-waist move. The tile publishes `_app/<target>/open`; a single in-process launcher consumes the `_app/*/open` pattern and spawns the mapped target scene.
- ratified: David, 2026-07-29 (DSD disposition).
- recommendation: intent-publish (the tile publishes `_app/<target>/open`; an in-process launcher consumes + spawns), consumed by ONE generalized launcher parameterized by a target->scene table rather than six sibling launchers.
- rationale: intent-publish preserves control-is-a-peer ([CXC-LB-CREDO]) — an Intelligence launches an app identically to a human — and it REUSES the exact seam the decisions/doc viewers already ride (`decisions_viewer_launcher.py`, [DX-NARROW-WAIST]). A generalized target->scene launcher is the narrow-waist move: one launcher + a data table, no six-fold fork. Direct launcher.py-style process spawn from the widget would break the peer symmetry (a widget-local spawn is not a bus event an Intelligence can issue) and duplicate the guard/dedupe/placement logic the launchers already own.
- alternatives: (a) six sibling launchers (more code, more drift surface); (b) the widget spawns the process directly (breaks control-is-a-peer, forks the guard logic).
- invalidating_assumption: that all seven targets are `runtime`-scene desktop windows spawnable by the shared launcher. If a target needs a fundamentally different spawn (e.g. a non-render-engine external process), that target gets its own launcher and this generalization is only partial.
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-LAUNCHBAR]

### [DD-LB-STORAGE-VIEWERS-HOME] The two storage viewers as nodes UNDER this spec (recommended) vs their own specs

- decision: where the Document Storage + Bus Storage viewers are specified.
- chosen: nodes UNDER this spec ([CXC-DOCNAV-*], [CXC-BUSNAV-*]), as authored — graduating to their own specs the moment either grows a WRITE/DELETE path.
- ratified: David, 2026-07-29 (DSD disposition).
- recommendation: nodes under this spec ([CXC-DOCNAV-*], [CXC-BUSNAV-*]) for now.
- rationale: they are small NAVIGATION SHELLS launched BY the Launch Bar, they share one shell-over-store pattern, and they add no renderer (they reuse the doc-viewer). Co-locating them with the ribbon that launches them keeps the tile->app story in one traversable place. They graduate to their own specs the moment they grow a WRITE/DELETE path ([CXC-DOCNAV-READONLY], [CXC-BUSNAV-READONLY]) — that is a real, separable capability with its own decisions.
- alternatives: two sibling specs now (more files, premature for read-only shells that are ~80% shared).
- invalidating_assumption: that both stay thin read/view shells. If either grows editing, promote it to its own spec.
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-LAUNCHBAR]

### [DD-LB-NEW-INTENTS] Mint six new `_app/<name>/open` intents + their launchers/scenes

- decision: six of the seven tiles ([CXC-LB-ROSTER]) need a NEW launch intent + launcher + target scene (`designer`, `harness`, `composer`, `docstore`, `busstore`, `bus`); only `_app/decisions/open` exists.
- chosen: APPROVED — mint the six new `_app/<name>/open` intents + the ONE generalized `target->scene` launcher (per [DD-LB-LAUNCH-MECHANISM]) + the target scenes, each with a by-construction register-guard test.
- ratified: David, 2026-07-29 (DSD disposition).
- recommendation: mint all six under the `_app/<name>/open` convention with a by-construction test that every roster intent resolves to a registered consumer ([CXC-DSDV-REGISTER] discipline). Sequence: `docstore`/`busstore` first (this spec fully defines their targets), then `harness`/`composer`/`bus`/`designer` (their target scenes already exist or are trivial wrappers — confirm each target scene path at ratify).
- rationale: the intent convention is proven; the missing piece is a consumer per target. A tile that publishes into the void ([CXC-LB-INTENT-TABLE] constraint) is an incomplete build, so the register-guard test is required, not optional.
- alternatives: only wire the tiles whose targets already have scenes and leave the rest as inert tiles (rejected — a dead tile is the silent-mask anti-pattern).
- invalidating_assumption: that each of the six targets is launchable as a `runtime` scene. Where a target is not (an external process), see [DD-LB-LAUNCH-MECHANISM].
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-LAUNCHBAR]

### [DD-LB-PROJECT-REGISTRY] Add three PROJECT entries (Launch Bar + the two viewer apps)

- decision: whether to register the Launch Bar and the two storage-VIEWER apps in `[REGISTRY:PROJECTS]` (`corpora/intelligence-console/projects.lts`).
- chosen: ADD the three `family: ComposeApps` entries — `[PROJECT:compose-launch-bar]`, `[PROJECT:document-storage-viewer]`, `[PROJECT:bus-storage-viewer]` — landed in `corpora/intelligence-console/projects.lts` (2026-07-29), DISTINCT from the existing storage-SERVICE entries `[PROJECT:document-store]` / `[PROJECT:bus-storage]`.
- ratified: David, 2026-07-29 (DSD disposition).
- recommendation: yes — three NEW `family: ComposeApps` entries: `[PROJECT:compose-launch-bar]`, `[PROJECT:document-storage-viewer]`, `[PROJECT:bus-storage-viewer]`. NOTE these are DISTINCT from the existing `[PROJECT:document-store]` / `[PROJECT:bus-storage]` entries, which are the STORAGE SERVICES (the doc:///bus:// servers, `family: ComposeBus Services`) — the viewers are new client APPS over those services, not the services.
- rationale: each is a new ComposeApp with its own root, decision-LTS point-forward, and specs pointer — the registry's stated purpose. Point-forward per [DEC-PROJECT-STRUCTURE]: register now, let each project's decision-LTS/specs be created as it matures.
- constraint: `projects.lts` is `machine-maintained: false` (human-reviewed). The three entries were added to the registry as part of this ratified disposition; David ratifies + lands via git-expert.
- alternatives: register only the Launch Bar (the viewers are nodes under this spec, so arguably not yet separable projects) — reasonable if [DD-LB-STORAGE-VIEWERS-HOME] keeps them as nodes.
- invalidating_assumption: that the registry convention wants an entry per launchable ComposeApp. If the convention is "one entry per repo/dir, not per app", fold the viewers under a single Launch Bar entry.
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-LAUNCHBAR]

